<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Wielder-side vehicle for UMW_NeedlePoint's hit-chance malus — the mod's only equipped hediff,
       and the idiomatic vehicle for a wielder STAT mod, not a workaround (full 1.6 decompile,
       2026-07-27): WeaponTraitDef.equippedStatOffsets is consumed in exactly two places in the
       assembly, both hardcoded to TryGetComp<CompBladelinkWeapon> (StatWorker.StatOffsetFromGear /
       GearHasCompsThatAffectStat) — silently inert on CompUniqueWeapon. The gear stat pipe is also
       offsets-only (gear can never contribute a factor) and its stat-breakdown line aggregates every
       offset on the item into one sum under the weapon's generated unique name, with no per-trait
       attribution. equippedHediffs, by contrast, are applied/removed by VANILLA's own
       WeaponTraitWorker.Notify_Equipped/Notify_EquipmentLost via CompUniqueWeapon — the only
       trait-granular wielder-stat vehicle it has, the only one supporting statFactors, and its
       breakdown line is named per-hediff ("needle-point grip: -2"). Don't migrate this to
       equippedStatOffsets. (A wielder effect that is a combat OUTCOME rather than a stat goes
       through its own mechanic instead — see MeleeParryExtension, which replaced the former
       UMW_ParryingGuard dodge hediff.)
       The -2 is in MeleeHitChance's UNFINALIZED units, not percent: hediff statOffsets are summed
       by StatWorker.GetValueUnfinalized and only then does FinalizeValue apply the stat's
       postProcessCurve — true of gear offsets too; StatDef.finalizeEquippedStatOffset only selects
       the DISPLAY style, never the math (exhaustive decompile grep, 2026-07-27). This stat's
       postProcessCurve ((-20,0.05) (-10,0.10) (0,0.50) (10,0.80) (20,0.90) (40,0.96) (60,0.98)) makes
       one raw point worth ~3pp of hit chance around melee 8 and ~1pp by melee 15, so -2 costs a green
       wielder ~6pp and an expert ~2pp: a delicate point is unforgiving to whoever hasn't mastered it.
       Anchored below Brawler's +4, the nearest Core offset to this stat. It has to bite, because it is
       the entire price of UMW_NeedlePoint's x1.2 damage-and-AP: an earlier -0.1 was written as though
       the field took a percentage, cost -0.3pp, and left that trait strictly good. The pairing nets
       +8% damage throughput at melee 4 rising to +17% at melee 19, and breaks exactly even at raw 0
       (x1.2 * 0.42/0.50 = 1.008) — strictly good with any skill, a wash for the utterly unskilled;
       confirmed at these values in the 2026-07 Odyssey balance pass. -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>UMW_NeedlePointGrip</defName>
    <label>needle-point grip</label>
    <description>The wielder has adapted their grip to a needle-fine point. The thrust drives deeper but is harder to land cleanly.</description>
    <hediffClass>Hediff</hediffClass>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <statOffsets>
          <MeleeHitChance>-2</MeleeHitChance> <!-- raw, pre-curve: ~-6pp at melee 8. cf. Brawler +4 -->
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
